      "message": "fix(sim): judge a gouge with tol of lateral slack at a wall\n\nThe program sim's gouge verdict (column engine `deviate` and field arm\n`deviate_field`) charged a column by height alone at its centre. A\nheight verdict's normal-distance tolerance is tol*cos(slope), zero at a\nvertical wall, so a column centre microns inside a wall, reached by a\ntool finishing that wall within tolerance, read as a gouge the wall's\nwhole height and the post gate refused a correct program.\n\nA gouge candidate is now judged against the lowest part top within tol\nof its centre (centre plus an eight-direction ring at radius tol; air\ncounts as lowest), in the new `stock_sim::wall_slack`, shared by both\nengines. A column past the slack still convicts at its centre's depth;\nrest is unchanged; a clean program pays nothing extra.\n\nOn the user's Milling-test.step: a 3D Finish (BN-0600) on model stock\nwas refused for 10.21 mm at (16.69, -24.91), a column 1-3 um inside the\nD's wall; in the 70x70x27 box stock for 37 cells, worst 22.01 mm. Both\nnow read 0 gouge cells.\n\nFixes #299\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
